Description
This repository contains the solutions for **Assignment 02** of the **Programming Fundamentals (PF)** course. The assignment includes six menu-driven C++ applications that demonstrate the use of functions, arrays, strings, loops, conditional statements, and modular programming. 
Programs Included
Program 01 - LESCO Billing System
* Customer Registration
* Electricity Bill Calculation
* GST, Income Tax & Fixed Charges
* New Connection Charges
* Customer Details
Program 02 - Restaurant Management System
* Customer Registration
* Food Menu
* Order Placement
* Bill Calculation
* Discounts & GST
* Customer Details
 Program 03 - Grocery Store Billing System
* Customer Registration
* Grocery Item Selection
* Cart Management
* Tax & Discounts
* Loyalty Points
* Final Bill Generation
 Program 04 - Online Shopping System
* User Registration
* Product Catalog
* Shopping Cart
* Delivery Charges
* GST & Discounts
* Checkout Bill
Program 05 - Social Media Campaign Management
* Client Registration
* Platform Selection
* Advertisement Budget
* Campaign Cost Calculation
* GST & Discounts
* Client Details
Program 06 - Personal Student Diary
* User Registration & Login
* Create Diary Entry
* View All Entries
* Read Entry
* Edit Entry
* Delete Single Entry
* Delete All Entries
 Concepts Covered
* Functions
* Arrays
* Strings
* Loops
* Conditional Statements
* Menu-Driven Programming
* Billing Systems
* User Authentication
* File-like Data Management using Arrays
 Language
 C++
 Compiler
* Dev-C++
* Visual Studio Code (GCC)
 How to Run
1. Open the C++ source code in your IDE.
2. Compile the program using a C++ compiler.
3. Run the executable file.
4. Follow the on-screen menu and enter the required inputs.
Learning Objectives
* Develop menu-driven applications
* Apply functions and modular programming
* Perform billing calculations
* Manage user input and output
* Improve problem-solving skills in C++
